# DTL Reader test timeline - covers every language feature.
# Open this file with a DTL theme active and try the autocomplete/hover
# scenarios listed in ../README.md.

#id:intro_line
join TestCharacter (LayeredPortrait) left [extra_data="set Head/LeftEye"]
TestCharacter (LayeredPortrait): Hello! [b]Welcome[/b] to the [i]test[/i] room. #id:greeting

# Hover over "TestCharacter" above (or on the join line below) to see its
# character documentation: display name "Super John", nicknames, description,
# and a colored title, all read from characters/TestCharacter.dch.

set {variable.test} = 2
TestCharacter: The test variable is {variable.test}, and Mamamya says {Mamamya}.
TestCharacter: Welcome to the Test Room! I'm out of mana, 0 MP left.[pause=0.5] [portrait=LayeredPortrait]<Oh well./Too bad./Never mind.>[aa]

Bare narration line with no character prefix, still gets [u]styled[/u] and [Shake]custom[/Shake] text.

join "John Smith" right
"John Smith": My name has a space in it, but I still get highlighted and colored correctly.
[wait time='1.5' skippable='true']
leave "John Smith"

update TestCharacter (Default) pos=x0.5 size=y1 [animation="Bounce" extra_data="set Head/RightEye"]
TestCharacter (Default): My mood just changed, {chapter} is the current chapter.

# Hover over "apply_tint" or "has_achievement" below to see their signature
# and ## documentation comment, read live from scripts/Global.gd.
do Global.has_achievement("")
if Global.has_achievement("intro_complete")
    TestCharacter: You've done this before!
elif not Global.has_achievement("intro_complete")
    TestCharacter: First time here, huh?

# Autoload members beyond functions: variables, constants and enums, plus an
# autoload NODE (SoundManager points at a .tscn - its root script is used).
do SoundManager.play_sfx("door_open")
set {Global.state} = Global.State.TALKING
if Global.state == Global.State.TALKING and Global.hearts < Global.MAX_HEARTS
    TestCharacter: You look hurt. You have {Global.hearts} hearts left.

TestCharacter: [color=red]Danger![/color] [wave amp=25 freq=5]Wheee[/wave][br]New line, [rainbow]fabulous[/rainbow].
TestCharacter: [b][i][rainbow freq=2]All at once[/rainbow][/i][/b], [outline_size=4][outline_color=black][color=yellow]outlined[/color][/outline_color][/outline_size], [fade start=2 length=8]fading away...[/fade] [hint="Hover me"]hint[/hint] [char=2665]

set {chapter} = 1
if {chapter} == 1
    TestCharacter: This is chapter {chapter}.
elif {chapter} == 2
    TestCharacter: Somehow chapter two.
else
    TestCharacter: Unknown chapter.

TestCharacter2: 

- Ask about the weather | #id:choice_weather
- Say goodbye | [if {chapter} == 1] #id:choice_goodbye

[wait time="1.0" skippable="true"]
[wait_input]
[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{\"Effect\":\"Rain\"}"]
[signal arg_type="dict" arg="{"type":"dice","c":"Laripo","s":false,"n":2}"]
[voice path="res://assets/voice_line.ogg"]
audio music "res://assets/theme.ogg"
[clear text="true"]
[background arg="res://assets/bg.png" transition="Simple Fade"]
[style name="default"]
[text_input text="Type something" var="{answer}" placeholder="..."]

## Loops back here until the chapter reaches 3.
## Hover "loop_start" in the jump below to read this.
label loop_start
while {chapter} < 3
    set {chapter} += 1
    jump loop_start

# Cross-timeline jumps: Ctrl+click either part to open chapter2.dtl.
- Go to chapter two
    jump chapter2/intro
- Go to its ending
    jump chapter2/Ending With Spaces

leave --All--
[end_timeline]
